  "limits": [
    "Only successful, consistent legacy registry state is transferred. Uncertain RUNNING/FAILED recovery is deliberately not inferred from timestamps.",
    "A generic owner-target receipt does not migrate or validate business dictionaries. Target-domain data adoption and installer handoff are still required.",
    "This local admin capability is not exposed via RPC or HTTP. Full installer operation persistence, identity mapping, old-client revocation and authenticated module caller policies remain incomplete.",
    "V2 must precede new registry binaries. Old executors/binaries must actually stop before transfer; a database marker does not fence old binaries that do not consult it.",
    "Registry transfer is atomic for one contribution only. It does not claim a cross-domain transaction or atomic whole-install batch.",
    "No production deployment, Consul configuration mutation, commit or push. Formal standalone and complete three-topology business acceptance remain pending."
  ]
